module ro_param_return.neg_1

// A `ro` PARAMETER RETURNED THROUGH A NON-`ro` RESULT (D246 amendment,
// E_READONLY_COERCE; registry 221.1 #1309). `x` is written without `mut`, so it
// is bound `ro` (D176), and `-> []int` would hand the caller a `mut w = f(v)`
// that writes what the parameter froze. The oracle refuses this program; novac
// accepted it without a word until 2026-09-23.
//
// This is the `=>` body. neg_2 is `return x` with a record, neg_3 a payload-free
// enum through an ordinary parameter of a method -- the three forms measured.

// NOVAC_EXPECT cannot return `x` through a result that is not `ro`

fn pass_through(x []int) -> []int => x

fn main() {
    println(1)
}
